WEBVTT

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.580
The world is awash in pain.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.290
Now, wars are fought between spies
over information -

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.250
in shadow wars.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.380
Time to decide who carries the backpack!

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.750
All right!

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.000
Most common choice wins!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.670
One, two, shoot!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.500
Damn it, Lily!
You said we'd choose rock together!

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.750
Huh? Is that what I said?

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.540
You assholes all played me!

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.830
I'm sure I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.080
I am sorry.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.830
You are the strongest one here, Sis.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.130
The pack's all yours!

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.500
I mean, I guess when you put it like that...

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.880
Everyone's gotten their jitters out, yeah?

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.460
It's time.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Honestly, I'm scared.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.960
I have this bad feeling that just won't go away.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.540
Like we're all making some sort
of horrible misunderstanding.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.460
It's going to be okay, Sara.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.080
You're not alone here.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.330
If something goes wrong,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.170
we'll put our heads together and come up with a plan.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.540
Miss Lily...

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.420
All right, Leader, time to go.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.830
Yup!

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.500
This battle is going to be Lamplight's big debut.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.330
Is everyone ready to put
their intensive training to the test?

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.040
Our infiltration routes will take us in
from the east and the west.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.750
I'll be operating separately from the rest of you.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.540
The sample we're after is somewhere
in this building here,

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.080
but we weren't able to track down an exact location.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.500
We'll have to go to the mission site
and get that intel in person.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.040
Abyss Doll...

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.000
I can't believe the Empire stole a killer virus.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.580
It spreads via airborne droplets over
its one-week incubation period,

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:04.880
then kills its host within twelve hours
of symptoms appearing.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.000
It's nothing short of evil incarnate.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.880
If they think they can get away with using bioweapons,
they've got another one coming.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.630
There are a number of soldiers and
Imperial spies stationed on-site.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.290
If they find you,
they'll shoot first and ask questions later.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.750
You'll need to deceive everyone
who stands in your way to take them down.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.920
There are three guards.
They're at range fifteen.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.460
Leave it to me, yo!

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.290
Oh no, you don't.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.670
Someone was able to escape
Mr. Bernard's surveillance?

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.250
That's gotta mean...

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.000
...we're dealing with a spy, and a good one.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.750
Let's do this!

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.750
Spread out! Quick!

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.750
<i>That bomb...</i>

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.830
<i>Its explosion was the same color
as the ones my mentor used to use.</i>

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.670
<i>Against him, I never once won a fight.</i>

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.000
<i>He was always a tenth of a second faster than me,
and I could never close that gap.</i>

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:17.000
<i>After Inferno got wiped out, I ID'd his corpse.</i>

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.250
<i>But what if it was a fake?</i>

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:42.000
<b>MISSION: Flower Garden III</b>

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.830
That's odd.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.920
My idiot pupil was supposed to be
the one coming in from the west.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.670
Did he change his mind at the last minute?

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.880
"Idiot pupil"?

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.290
Well, this works.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:49.670
Once I take all seven of these kids hostage,
that will be that.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.000
It can't be...

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.540
You're Teach's mentor, Mr. Guido?

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.080
What the hell? You know my name?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.540
That Klaus has got some loose lips.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.750
But how?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.670
Everyone on Inferno is supposed to be dead.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.540
He turned traitor.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:06.750
He betrayed his team.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.330
I always thought it was weird.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.380
Impossible Mission or not,

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.580
it doesn't make sense for a team that legendary
to go down so easily.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.170
But how did you know our infiltration route?

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:19.960
You're not the brightest, are you?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.790
I was on Inferno,

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.250
so I used to live in Heat Haze Palace.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:28.630
I bugged the place to the gills myself.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.830
Is it starting to make sense, little ladies?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.290
We heard everything through the wiretap.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:39.210
I know everything about you seven,
and I know your entire plan.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.790
If we run, he'll just capture us one by one.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.000
Instead, we should take him on together.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.750
Agreed.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.500
Seven on one, huh?

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.710
You're all going down.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.960
Unfortunately for you,

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.500
we've got loads of practice fighting while outmatched!

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.330
Wires, huh?

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.880
What are you...

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.290
dumb or something?!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.290
Annette!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.500
Remember where you learned that trap?

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.750
The Republic's spy techniques won't work on me.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:28.630
Six left.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.580
Welcome to hell, kiddos.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:36.460
Blue Fly has made contact with enemy spies
by the western pipeline block.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.330
Then our information was accurate.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.130
Our counterintelligence department
never fails to impress.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.330
I have a report.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.630
The hostile coming from the east

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.960
is heading straight for us here in the main building,
just as we planned.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:53.000
He might not look it, but he's a total softie.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:56.330
He's probably freaking out right about now.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.420
He's thinking, "I can't afford to lose another team,"
or something like that.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.630
Now, come on out.
You have ten seconds.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.540
For every second past that, I break one of her fingers.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:10.670
Buy us some time.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.920
We'll use it to prepare our next move.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.540
You sure made up your mind quickly.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.000
It was the wrong call, though.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.000
You should've abandoned your friend and fled.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.710
We made a decision.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.630
We decided that all seven of us
would make it out alive.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:34.670
Lamplight wouldn't be Lamplight
without Teach and seven hotties like me.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.080
A rainbow's got seven colors,
and there are seven deadly sins.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.040
It's the perfect number.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:44.000
We've got me for greed, Thea for lust,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.750
Sybilla for wrath-

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.040
Who you callin' "Wrath"?!

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.460
She just had throw in that bit
calling herself a hottie, huh?

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.210
Having six or eight of us wouldn't feel right.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.670
The seven of us are all going to go back,
together with Teach!

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.040
We're ready.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.710
<i>What a headache.</i>

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:17.960
No-

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.380
Stay back!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.380
Stay back!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.710
I guess that'd make you "Lust," huh?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.580
If you're trying to bait me, it won't work.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.460
How cold.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:33.330
Still, you were too slow!

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.250
Magnificent.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:37.830
This is checkmate, Guido!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:40.380
You seriously thought that disguise would fool me?

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:51.130
He always calls me "Master."

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.040
Five left.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.040
Four left.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.380
Thanks, you two.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.830
Now, get him!

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.290
What was that, a paralyzing agent?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.040
You must have some sort of poison resistance.

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.420
But so what?
We've got this!<b></b>

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.540
Three left.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.210
No way...

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.790
My poison didn't work?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.750
Sure it did.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:31.040
I held my breath as fast as I could,
but it still stings like hell.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:34.040
See? I can barely feel my fingertips.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:43.830
Two left.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.790
Run, Miss Lily!

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.290
One left.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:03.630
You son of a...

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.130
How dare you hurt my friends?!

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.460
Sorry, kid.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:15.000
All that work you did this past month was for nothing.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.580
Zero left.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.040
A wall?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.000
Too bad, so sad.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:29.960
All that information you gathered was
bad intel we fed you on purpose.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.130
You must be an Imperial spy.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:38.040
Blue Fly, or as you knew him, Guido, turned traitor.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.040
And when he did, we got full dossiers
on every spy the Din Republic has.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.080
There's no way in hell you could beat us-

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.750
A trap? But when?

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:00.500
I have some questions for you.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.790
And I expect answers.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.460
I figured out what you're after.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:18.540
It's Teach, right?

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.750
He's been your target all along.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:22.750
Bingo!

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.250
Here's the low-down for you.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:29.540
When we took out Inferno two months ago,
the plan was for him to die, too.

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:33.880
I gave him a special mission to
isolate him from the group.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:37.170
Him teaming up with the others
would have been a problem.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.580
Back then, I was being sarcastic.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:43.540
I knew that there was no way he was
making it out of there alive.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:47.710
But then, imagine my surprise
when the little bastard pulled through.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:52.920
I sent waves of top-notch Imperial spies after him,
and he put them all in the ground.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:57.710
As far as the Empire's concerned,
getting rid of him is a top priority.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.880
And so-

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.500
You used Abyss Doll as bait to lure him out.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:03.000
Right again.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.540
Not even he's going to be able to survive this.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.380
When he hears that, he'll come running.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.250
That's how much he cares about his teammates.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.330
Faced with an opponent he can't beat

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:20.920
and the disadvantage of having seven of his students
taken hostage, he'll fight valiantly...

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.250
and perish.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.790
You've got it all figured out.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:34.630
If Teach comes, he'll die,
and if he doesn't, you'll kill us.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.170
Oh no! Whatever will we do?!

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.710
I have to ask, Mr. Guido...

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:44.080
How much longer should I keep
playing along with this game?

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.500
Can you hear me, Master?

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.540
It's been a while.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.210
I just secured the Abyss Doll sample.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.920
The mission is complete.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:01.080
All that's left for me to do is escape.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.920
<b>MISSION: Flower Garden III</b>

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.880
We're about to head to the mission site,

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:13.380
but in all likelihood,  the Empire will be expecting us.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.580
However, that's not a problem.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.710
We'll go in pretending we're none the wiser.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:23.380
Thinking we know nothing, our enemies will
underestimate us and try to catch me in a trap.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:27.580
Then, I can turn the tables on them
and secure the intel we need.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.750
So, what's our job?

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:32.080
There's one foe in particular I need you to deceive.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:35.170
So, we're a diversion, Boss?

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:36.710
Exactly.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.830
By feigning weakness, you can create an opening.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:41.670
That's your true mission.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.580
Did you hear me, Master?

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:47.420
I'm taking the Abyss Doll sample and going home.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.790
Even if I came over there, I can't beat you in a fight.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.920
It makes more sense for me to prioritize the mission.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.330
Cut the crap!

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.500
If you're not here in five minutes-

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.580
Oh, and Master,

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.250
you're working under a large misconception.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.830
I always suspected that one of Inferno's members
had turned traitor.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:11.460
I knew it was an inside job since the moment
I heard the news two months ago.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:14.040
There was no proof.
How could you-

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.250
I just did.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.540
If I had to give a reason, though,

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:22.290
it was because I found those bugs
you planted in Heat Haze Palace.

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.330
Wait, you found them?!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.330
I did.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:29.880
That's why the seven girls there and I
operated under the assumption

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:32.750
that a traitor was listening to
everything we did in Heat Haze Palace.

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:37.540
When we first met, I gave them a set
of Communal Living Rules.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.630
For example, one of them was as follows:

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.750
Never use your unique talents
inside Heat Haze Palace.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.710
When the girls read the rules,
they understood what I was getting at.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:52.380
From there, they spent the next month
faithfully obeying them.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:57.250
In other words, Master, you think you know
what the girls are capable of,

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.080
but the truth is, you know nothing.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.710
The dossiers you have on every
full-fledged spy in the Republic

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:06.210
won't do you a bit of good
against the academies' girl wonders.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:11.250
Each member of Lamplight has
a deadly skill they keep hidden away.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.790
I can say with full confidence that
the girls will defeat you.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:20.460
I'm code name Flower Garden,
and it's time to bloom out of control.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.130
It smells so acrid...

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.380
Is that foam what I think it is?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.380
Yup!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.540
This poison foam takes full advantage
of my abnormal physiology.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.540
I spent this past month coming up with it.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.750
And you don't know a thing about it.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.830
Want to try it on?

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:41.790
You washouts still don't stand a chance against me.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.580
Why even bother getting up?

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.670
Because it feels real nice.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.500
You wouldn't get it.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:53.710
Someone who chose to betray the family
they lived with in Heat Haze Palace never could.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.420
This is for the others, and also...

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.830
it's for the ideals Teach is still carrying.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.040
I'm taking you down, Mr. Guido!

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.210
Too slow.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.040
It was just for show?
Figures.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:31.290
Can you hear me, Klaus?

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.580
I took out all seven of 'em!

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:36.080
Your students are all-

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:45.920
Was that an accident?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.750
It can't just be a coincidence.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.250
How unlucky...

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:57.830
<i>She was hiding in the white-haired kid's backpack?</i>

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.830
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:03.790
Our first coordinated plan,
and I get stuck with the hardest job.

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.670
There was an eighth?

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:06.880
Indeed there was.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:11.790
The eight girls had to live
as if they were seven people.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:16.960
That was one of the orders I gave them
via the Communal Living Rules.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:19.080
Allow me to introduce her.

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:20.880
She is...

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.380
Lamplight's eighth member.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.920
<b>Fool</b>

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.630
I'm Erna.

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:29.500
On the first day,

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.670
Lily and the rest of the original seven
were the only ones who arrived.

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.420
But on the morning of the second day,

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:37.130
Erna showed up late and
joined the roster as its eighth member.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:41.330
From that point on, they went about their lives
making sure never to mention

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.210
that there were actually eight of them.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:46.040
It was a trick built around the wiretap.

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:52.080
Seeing them in person would have made it obvious
that there were eight of them,

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:56.210
but it's hard to tell eight girls apart
by their voices alone.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.290
Erna specializes in misfortune,

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.630
and she's an expert when it comes to
accidents and disasters.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:04.790
Her sharp senses let her subconsciously
pick up on portents of doom,

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.790
allowing her to get others caught up in them.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.580
There's no way...

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:09.880
Oh, but there is.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.790
She's our super secret ace in the hole.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:14.080
Yeep.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:18.000
How many lies did you pile up?

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:25.500
You seriously sacrificed a month of your lives
just to land a single attack?

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.630
Just how far did you-

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:34.080
We seriously did.
We're your idiot pupil's pupils, after all.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.460
The plan worked.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.670
Yup!

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.130
Now, we can leave the rest to Teach and-

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.380
Behind you!

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:03.790
But my stab landed, I know it did!

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:06.920
Yeah, I even passed out for a second.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.210
I gotta hand it to you.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.830
It's been a while since that happened.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:15.830
My moves are a tenth of a second slower.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.080
That was all your efforts amounted to.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:20.330
No way! That's it?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.960
That's all we accomplished?

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:24.750
Magnificent.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:33.170
There you are, Idiot Pupil.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.380
Abyss Doll is in here.

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:40.330
Take it and go.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.670
You got it all on your own?

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.040
I couldn't have done it
if you all hadn't distracted my mentor.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:50.000
I might be a bit.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.580
Go on ahead and take escape route four back to Din.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:57.250
And like a fountain welling up from a plateau,
remember your training.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.500
That doesn't make sense, but you got it!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.540
That was some excellent work my students did.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.830
Your movements are a tenth of a second slower.

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:24.000
I finally caught up.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.710
Don't get cocky on me, Idiot Pupil.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.750
I'm sorry, Master,

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:35.750
but in your current state,
you aren't qualified to be my enemy.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:41.210
Impossible Missions have
a ninety percent mortality rate,

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:48.580
but us eight Lamplight girls made it through ours
without losing a single member.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.750
Then, a week later...

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:57.000
Thanks for everything, Teach.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.420
So, the eight of them
all went back to their academies?

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.880
That's right.

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:07.710
Lamplight was a provisional team assembled
to complete a single Impossible Mission.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.420
Now that the mission's over,
it makes sense to disband the team.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:16.250
They won't have to self-deprecatingly
call themselves washouts anymore.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:21.500
If they can go forward with their heads held high,
then I could ask for nothing more.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:24.290
You almost sound like a real teacher.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.500
Please.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.580
As an instructor, I was incompetent from start to finish.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.290
Really, now?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:33.420
I wonder what your mentor
would have to say about that?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.670
What became of Guido's body?

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:47.420
Sadly, this is all I was able to
bring back with me from the Empire.

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:54.790
Why did you betray Inferno, Master?

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.830
End it.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:02.500
Finish the job, Klaus.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.920
I'm not letting you die, not yet.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.420
I'm going to be disbanding Lamplight.

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:12.250
The two of us can rebuild Inferno together, Master.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.250
You can atone for what you did

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.290
by putting your life on the line
for the country we all love.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.290
What are you...

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:23.880
You're the only family I have left, Guido.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.750
You're too soft, kid.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:34.670
Was that a sniper scope just now?

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:37.500
Master!

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:45.330
Make sure you protect 'em this time...

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:55.920
<i>Who was it?
Who took the shot?</i>

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.960
We finally caught you!

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:05.460
Wait...

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:07.790
Aren't you supposed to be back at your academies?

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:09.040
We were acting!

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:11.000
Because we're spies, yo!

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:13.170
I'm sorry, Boss.

00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:16.380
At long last, our victory is at hand!

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:18.920
Now, we can make whatever demands we want.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.210
What demands?

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:21.790
Do you even have to ask?

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:24.250
We want Lamplight to stay together.

00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:27.750
We all talked it over.

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:31.580
And, um, instead of going back to
our academies, graduating,

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:34.500
and getting stuck on teams with a bunch of strangers...

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:38.250
...we figured we would rather stick with the people
we'd already been in the foxhole with.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:41.630
You could have just asked normally.

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:46.580
Why bother tricking me, locking me up,
and holding me at gunpoint?

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:48.460
We're just continuing your lesson plan.

00:22:48.460 --> 00:22:50.290
That class has concluded.

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:51.920
Call it payback, then.

00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:53.290
You surrender, right?

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:55.380
We want to keep learning from you.

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:59.830
Teach us how a bunch of former washouts
can come into bloom.

00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:01.210
Yeah.

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:10.580
Make sure you protect 'em this time.

00:23:12.460 --> 00:23:14.210
I see where you're coming from.

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:15.420
However...

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:19.580
It's as you can see.

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:23.580
You aren't qualified to be my enemies yet.

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:24.790
But that aside...

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.040
Magnificent.

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:37.250
Then for all seven of you on Lamplight,
class is back in session.

00:23:37.630 --> 00:23:39.710
All eight, I should say.
